      "independent_solution": "Reuse my immutable text source-solutions-FIRST.record (21056 bytes, SHA-256 00ac72b76e98430315ae33101c800198aaac4c82d76291b63e09e700c69af713), U1--U3, without re-solving. 1/|x| has domain x!=0 and two positive reflected reciprocal branches: -1/x on x<0, 1/x on x>0, no axis intercept, limits +infinity at zero and 0+ at infinite tails. 1/sqrt(x) has domain x>0 only, a positive decreasing convex branch through (1/4,2),(1,1),(4,1/2), no origin or negative branch. x^3/|x| retains x!=0 after simplification: -x^2 on x<0, x^2 on x>0, odd increasing branches and the exact removable hole (0,0), not a filled extension. These independently frozen solutions agree with the newly disclosed author source record.",
