      "independent_solution": "Reuse frozen U4--U7 from the same source receipt. All four domains are R. sqrt(x^2)=|x|, so plus x gives y=0 on x<=0 and y=2x on x>=0; minus x gives y=-2x on x<=0 and y=0 on x>=0, both with included O and whole zero half-rays. Their minimum zero is attained on an entire half-line, not solely at the vertex. |x+2| is the upward unit-slope V with included vertex (-2,0), a left-two horizontal shift and y-intercept 2. |x-1| is the upward unit-slope V with included vertex (1,0), a right-one shift and y-intercept 1. Both V graphs have range [0,infinity), unique included minima, no holes and diverging tails. Author derivations agree.",
