      "independent_solution": "Reuse frozen U8, without re-solving. Domain x!=0; f(x)=x+1/x has the sign of x, odd disconnected branches and no axis intercept. Positive branch has included minimum (1,2); negative branch has included maximum (-1,-2), neither a global extremum of the entire unbounded function. Range=(-infinity,-2] union [2,infinity). Branches respectively decrease/increase around x=1 and increase/decrease around x=-1. x=0 is a vertical asymptote with negative/positive infinite limits from left/right. y=x is oblique because f-x=1/x; negative tail is below it and positive tail above it. Actual 640 B has the same two branches and extrema; dashed Guide is not part of the function. Author source/key/rationale agree with these frozen facts.",
